---
import bayphl1 from "../../assets/1/banner.svg";
import packet1 from "../../assets/1/packet-1-start.pdf";
import packet2 from "../../assets/1/packet-2-beta.pdf";
import packet3 from "../../assets/1/packet-3-gamma.pdf";
import packet4 from "../../assets/1/packet-4-beta-revisited.pdf";
import packet5 from "../../assets/1/packet-5-alpha-revisited.pdf";
import packet6 from "../../assets/1/packet-6-end.pdf";
import puzzleTheLostBooks from "../../assets/1/puzzles/the-lost-books/puzzle.pdf";
import puzzleSupplyChains from "../../assets/1/puzzles/supply-chains/puzzle.pdf";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link
      href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/modern-css-reset@1.4.0/dist/reset.min.css"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>BayPHL 1</title>
  </head>

  <body>
    <div id="root">
      <div id="header">
        <div class="tabs">
          <a href="#info">Summary</a>
          <a href="#puzzles">Puzzles</a>
          <a href="#credits">Credits</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="banner"><img src={bayphl1.src} alt="BayPHL 1" /></div>

      <div class="block">
        <a href="/"><strong>← Back to BayPHL homepage</strong></a>
      </div>

      <div class="block" id="info">
        <h1>BayPHL 1</h1>

        <p>
          BayPHL 1 took place on November 8th and 9th, 2025 in the Marina
          District of San Francisco. A total of 75 teams participated. Thanks to
          everyone who joined us, and a special congratulations to the teams
          that finished:

          <details style="margin-bottom: 1em;">
            <summary>Finishing teams (in alphabetical order)</summary>

            <ul>
              <li>✈✈✈</li>
              <li>🚀🚀🚀</li>
              <li>Baffled</li>
              <li>Big Dipper</li>
              <li>BMT</li>
              <li>Capybara Collective</li>
              <li>Casual Birders</li>
              <li>Chicken and ROFLs</li>
              <li>Consumer Recreation Services</li>
              <li>Cult of Idiotic Avians</li>
              <li>Duck Gizzards</li>
              <li>dunno</li>
              <li>frak overspill not yet a health concern</li>
              <li>gaylactic trendysetters</li>
              <li>glwacoy</li>
              <li>Golden Delicious</li>
              <li>happy birthday jon!</li>
              <li>Have you tried moving to the Bay Area?</li>
              <li>Lake Supreme</li>
              <li>Leguminati</li>
              <li>Literally Baffle Waffle</li>
              <li>LXP</li>
              <li>Owls in Towels</li>
              <li>Peanut Butter & Jellyfish</li>
              <li>Pinniped Party</li>
              <li>Ship of Fools</li>
              <li>Something's Fishy</li>
              <li>Strobe Light Syzygy</li>
              <li>Team Locurio</li>
              <li>Team Prospect</li>
              <li>tfti</li>
              <li>The Last Minute Tram</li>
              <li>We are the issue</li>
            </ul>
          </details>
        </p>

        <p>
          <em
            >(Did you finish BayPHL 1 but aren’t credited above? Email us and
            let us know at <a href="mailto:bayphl1@bayphl.org"
              >bayphl1@bayphl.org</a
            >. We did our best but the beer may have distracted us a little from
            marking things off in our tracker.)</em
          >
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="block" id="puzzles">
        <h2>Puzzles and Solutions</h2>

        <p>
          BayPHL 1 was an adaptation of <a href="https://24.baphl.org"
            >BAPHL 24</a
          > for the San Francisco Bay Area. As with BAPHL, teams of newly minted
          archaeologists were sent out to investigate well-known wonders of the world
          and see if they could unearth any secrets (Beginner Archaeologists — Yay!
          — Pursuing Historical Landmarks). Starting in Fort Mason, teams traversed
          the Marina District of San Francisco to the Palace of the Fine Arts, where
          they solved their first metapuzzle and learned their first big secret.
          That enabled them to return to sites they had already visited, discovering
          new wonders along the way, before ending at Ghirardelli Square, where they
          received their final metapuzzle.
        </p>

        <p>
          BayPHL 1 consisted of 21 puzzles, broken into two rounds. The first
          round included 6 “major wonders” and 6 “minor wonders,” (puzzles which
          leveraged specific locations, physical components, or temporary
          installations), capped off by a metapuzzle. The second round featured
          7 additional puzzles and a capstone metapuzzle.
        </p>

        <p>
          Here are the puzzles from BayPHL 1, grouped into the stops where teams
          collected them:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li><a href={packet1}>Packet 1: Start</a></li>
          <li><a href={packet2}>Packet 2: Beta</a></li>
          <li><a href={packet3}>Packet 3: Gamma</a></li>
          <li><a href={packet4}>Packet 4: Beta Revisited</a></li>
          <li><a href={packet5}>Packet 5: Alpha Revisited</a></li>
          <li><a href={packet6}>Packet 6: End</a></li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Most of the puzzles were taken directly from BAPHL 24, occasionally
          with very light modifications (for instance, eliminating a clue about
          “Camber-ville” which might not land this far away from Cambridge). For
          BAPHL, we offered teams the option signing up for either “normal” or
          “hard” difficulty. As a logistical optimization for BayPHL, we only
          produced a single difficulty which blended the two modes. Rather than
          reproduce the solutions for those puzzles, <a
            href="https://24.baphl.org">check out the BAPHL 24 solutions</a
          >.
        </p>

        <p>
          Here are the solutions for the two puzzles that we created for BayPHL
          1 (replacing “Young Kid Yoga: A Park Day” and ”Field Trip” from
          BAPHL):
        </p>

        <table class="puzzles">
          <tr>
            <td class="title">The Lost Books</td>
            <td class="byline">Evan Broder, James Douberley</td>
            <td class="link">
              <a href={puzzleTheLostBooks} target="_blank">Puzzle</a>
            </td>
            <td class="link">
              <a href="./puzzles/the-lost-books/solution.html">Solution</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="title">Supply Chains</td>
            <td class="byline">Jessen Yu</td>
            <td class="link">
              <a href={puzzleSupplyChains} target="_blank">Puzzle</a>
            </td>
            <td class="link"
              ><a href="./puzzles/supply-chains/solution.html">Solution</a></td
            >
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="location-info" colspan="4">
              Supply Chains was a location puzzle, which required teams to find
              the <a
                href="https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/world-sources-of-food-mural"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer">World Sources of Food mosaic</a
              > on the side of the Safeway on Marina Boulevard.
            </td>
          </tr>
        </table>

        <div class="block" id="credits">
          <h2>Credits</h2>
        </div>

        <div class="block" id="contact">
          Questions? Comments? Please reach out to us at
          <a href="mailto:bayphl1@bayphl.org">bayphl1@bayphl.org</a>.
        </div>
      </div>

      <style is:global>
        :root {
          --color-rust: #a0522d;
          --color-cream: #f5f5dc;
          --color-sand: #f4e4c1;
          --color-espresso: #3c2414;
          --color-slate-300: #2b3d4f;
          --color-slate-500: #486684;
          --color-sage-100: #1f2519;
          --color-sage-200: #3f4b32;
          --color-sage-300: #5e704b;
          --color-sage-400: #7d9564;
          --color-sage-500: #9caf88;
          --color-sage-600: #b0bfa0;
          --color-sage-700: #c4cfb7;
          --color-sage-800: #d7dfcf;
          --color-sage-900: #ebefe7;

          font-family: "Inter", sans-serif;

          --color-background: var(--color-sand);
          --color-surface: var(--color-cream);
          --color-text: var(--color-espresso);
          --color-border: var(--color-rust);
          --color-link: var(--color-slate-500);
          --color-link-hover: var(--color-slate-300);
          --color-tab-hover: var(--color-sage-700);
        }

        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
          :root {
            --color-background: var(--color-espresso);
            --color-surface: var(--color-rust);
            --color-text: var(--color-sand);
            --color-border: #8b6f42; /* Warmer brown border instead of slate */
            --color-link: var(--color-sage-700);
            --color-link-hover: var(--color-sage-500);
            --color-tab-hover: var(--color-sage-200);
          }
        }

        html,
        body {
          margin: 0;
          padding: 0;
        }

        body {
          background: var(--color-background);
          color: var(--color-text);
          min-height: 100vh;
          display: flex;
          flex-direction: column;
        }
      </style>

      <style>
        @import url("https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:ital,opsz,wght@0,14..32,100..900;1,14..32,100..900&family=Roboto+Slab:wght@100..900&display=swap");

        h1,
        h2,
        h3,
        h4,
        h5,
        h6,
        .tabs a {
          font-family: "Roboto Slab", serif;
          font-weight: bold;
          color: var(--color-text);
        }

        h1 {
          font-weight: 900;
        }

        h2 {
          border-bottom: 1px solid #000000;
          margin-bottom: 0.5em;
        }

        p {
          margin-bottom: 1rem;

          &:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 0;
          }
        }

        a {
          color: var(--color-link);
        }

        a:hover {
          color: var(--color-link-hover);
        }

        dt {
          font-weight: bold;
        }
        dd {
          margin-bottom: 5px;
          margin-left: 25px;
          margin-top: 5px;
        }

        p,
        dd {
          line-height: 1.55;
        }

        #root {
          max-width: 980px;
          min-height: 100vh;
          margin-inline: auto;
          display: flex;
          flex-direction: column;
          padding-top: 20px;
        }

        #header {
          padding-bottom: 8px;
        }

        #banner {
          width: 100%;
          max-width: 690px;
          margin: 20px auto;
        }

        .block {
          margin-bottom: 8px;
          margin-top: 0px;
          background: var(--color-surface);
          border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
          padding: 15px;
        }

        .tabs {
          display: flex;
          gap: 0.5ex;
          justify-content: end;
          flex-wrap: wrap;

          > * {
            border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
            padding: 5px 10px;
            background: var(--color-surface);
          }

          a {
            text-decoration: none;
          }

          a:hover {
            background-color: var(--color-tab-hover);
          }
        }

        .puzzles {
          border-collapse: collapse;
          width: 100%;
          margin-bottom: 1em;

          td.title {
            width: 40%;
          }

          td.byline {
            width: 40%;
          }

          td.link {
            text-align: right;
            width: 10%;
          }

          .location-info {
            font-size: 0.8em;
            font-style: italic;
          }
        }
      </style>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
